    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Class: topical (dorzolamide, brinzolamide) + oral (acetazolamide, methazolamide)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Open-angle glaucoma: ⍺2 agonist (eg brimonidine) or CAI (eg acetazolamide) if prostaglandin analogs + beta-blockers are CI; acetazolamide + brimonidine = adjunctive or 2nd-line"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Angle-closure glaucoma: IV acetazolamide + topical pilocarpine, apraclonidine, + timolol"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    CRAO: IV acetazolamide to ⇣IOP"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    IIH/papilledema: acetazolamide first line (⇣CSF production) + wt loss"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Ménière dz: a diuretic (eg acetazolamide, triamterene-HCTZ) or chronic betahistine for preventative mgmt (w/ ⇣Na, caffeine, alcohol, nicotine, + MSG)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    SE (oral): transient myopia, N/V/diarrhea, ⇣appetite + taste, paresthesia, lassitude, kidney stones, + hematological problems; topical = much less systemic (local irritation + redness)"
     }
    ]
   }
